import pathlib,json,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];N={n['id']:n for n in json.loads((R/'data/notes.json').read_text())};aliases=json.loads((R/'research/edition-09-id-map.json').read_text())
def ref(i):return aliases['E9-2602-'+str(i).zfill(3)]
rows='''1~A comparison says Union expenditure rose7.7%. Which check is essential?~That the comparison uses FY2025–26 Revised Estimates, not a different baseline.~That it measures7.7% real growth by definition.|That the deficit target was already achieved.|That expenditure excludes every capital item.
2~January’s old-series7.4% and February’s new-series7.6% estimates should be:~Preserved with their different base years,estimate vintages and methodology.~Spliced as identical-method final outcomes.|Treated as proof exactly0.2% new output was physically created by rebasing.|Averaged to create an official estimate.
3~Double deflation estimates real value added by:~Separately treating output and intermediate-input price changes.~Subtracting the same inflation rate twice from nominal GDP.|Using only consumer prices for every sector.|Eliminating every future statistical revision.
4~On12February,the first CPI2024 release’s2.75% figure represented:~January2026 provisional combined year-on-year inflation.~February2026 final inflation.|The absolute price-index level.|A guarantee of the eventual final January value.
5~Consider three statements about February’s decision:1.Repo5.25%.2.SDF5%.3.Neutral stance guarantees the next move is a cut. Which are correct?~1and2only.~1and3only.|2and3only.|1,2and3.
6~A Budget proposes a biologics ecosystem and trial-site network. This alone establishes:~Proposed capacity support,not automatic approval of every biosimilar.~All trial sites are operational.|Every biological medicine is a simple generic equivalent.|Every safety requirement is waived.
7~A state announces a semiconductor partnership after ISM2.0. Which inference needs separate evidence?~That a specific fabrication plant has been commissioned.~That materials/equipment are distinct from chip design.|That training can complement investment.|That supply-chain depth matters.
8~A small supplier discounts an accepted invoice on TReDS. This is principally:~Receivables finance,distinct from an equity investment under a growth fund.~An equal unconditional grant to all MSMEs.|A completed purchase of a semiconductor fab.|The same transaction as a startup fund-of-funds commitment.
9~The accepted41% vertical-devolution recommendation means:~The states collectively receive the specified share of net divisible Union tax proceeds.~Each state receives41% of gross Union revenue.|All cesses automatically enter the pool.|Every other Commission recommendation is accepted without qualification.
10~Consider:1.Entry conditions include constituted bodies/accounts.2.States should pass grants within ten working days.3.Untied means salaries and all establishment spending are unrestricted. Which are correct?~1and2only.~2and3only.|1and3only.|1,2and3.
11~The ₹2,04,401crore state disaster-fund corpus should not be described as:~Entirely a Union contribution,with no state financing component.~A multi-year allocation.|A corpus covering response and mitigation funds.|Distinct from national-level disaster funds.
12~Which pairing is correct?~CDS—specified credit-event protection;TRS—transfer of total return exposure.~CDS—risk-free deposit;TRS—automatic government grant.|CDS—ordinary share ownership;TRS—cash reserve ratio.|CDS—guaranteed full bond ownership;TRS—elimination of counterparty risk.
13~A February REIT lending consultation lists proposed eligibility rules. What is the safest interpretation?~Check the final operative directions before treating every proposal as binding.~Every REIT immediately acquired an unrestricted right to bank credit.|Every InvIT investment is government guaranteed.|A consultation deadline itself commissions an infrastructure asset.
14~A40% bank capital-market-exposure ceiling is:~A prudential exposure limit,not a universal borrower loan-to-value entitlement.~A guaranteed40% subsidy for every acquisition.|The same as a40% repo rate.|Proof every bank can ignore borrower eligibility.
15~After the7February US framework and later legal events,which is justified?~Use a dated product/legal-authority check rather than assume18% remained a universal permanent tariff.~Every export permanently faced exactly18%.|Every conditional removal was completed on7February.|The$500billion purchase intention was already fully spent.
16~India–GCC terms of reference establish:~Negotiating scope/modalities,not a concluded operative FTA.~Immediate unrestricted tariff-free trade with every West Asian country.|Automatic replacement of all bilateral agreements.|GCC membership of every Asian economy.
17~Two announcements each mention ₹10,000crore. The Startup Fund of Funds2.0 and SME Growth Fund are:~Distinct instruments whose corpus and delivery channels should not be merged.~The same compulsory individual grant.|A single completed expenditure entry.|Turnover thresholds for ordinary startup recognition.
18~Consider:1.General turnover threshold₹200crore.2.Deep-tech age/turnover thresholds20years/₹300crore.3.Cooperatives qualify automatically without other conditions. Which are correct?~1and2only.~1and3only.|2and3only.|1,2and3.
19~DAC clears proposals with a large aggregate value. This is not equivalent to:~All contracts signed,equipment delivered and expenditure incurred.~An acquisition-stage decision.|A basis for later procurement scrutiny.|An opportunity to assess life-cycle support.
23~A hypothetical eligible urban project costs₹100crore. Which financing package matches the reviewed headline conditions?~₹25crore central assistance,₹50crore market finance and₹25crore local/state contribution.~₹100crore central grant and no market finance.|₹25crore central assistance and₹75crore mandatory grant from an unrelated state.|₹25crore central assistance and₹10crore market finance with no other qualifying market financing.
24~The Industrial Relations amendment should be read as:~A repeal-date clarification linked to November2025,with passage distinguished from other legal stages.~Proof all four Labour Codes first began in February2026.|Abolition of every worker remedy.|A substitute for every final subordinate rule.
26~The New Delhi AI declaration’s reviewed character is:~Voluntary/non-binding international cooperation,not a global enforceable AI statute.~A universal mandatory treaty automatically displacing national law.|Proof exactly91 will remain the endorsement count forever.|An exemption from all domestic data safeguards.
28~The reviewed offshore-mineral rules cover:~Specified offshore minerals,excluding mineral oils/hydrocarbons.~All petroleum under an identical carrier permit.|Every unregistered vessel automatically.|Extraction without any operating right merely because a transit form exists.
29~An eligible PM RAHAT case receives:~Cashless treatment within the₹1.5lakh/up-to-seven-day limits,not an unrestricted lump-sum award.~₹1.5lakh cash regardless of treatment cost.|Unlimited care for seven years.|A requirement that all care always wait48hours before beginning.
30~Which statement correctly separates rural and urban institutions?~The three-tier panchayat structure should not be copied as an identical mandatory municipal hierarchy.~Every municipality must have the same three tiers as a panchayat.|A schedule listing29subjects automatically devolves all staff/funds.|Local elections are irrelevant to grant eligibility.
31~To judge a Lakhpati Didi livelihood outcome,one should distinguish:~Sustained household income,individual control,turnover,profit and debt.~Every enrolment from guaranteed income success.|₹1lakh earned from an automatic₹1lakh state cash grant.|Sales revenue from profit as identical measures.
33~Which comparison is conceptually sound?~Warehouse capacity is a stock/space measure;annual production and throughput are flows.~Annual production must always equal central-pool storage capacity.|Every household store is counted in FCI capacity.|Announced credit targets equal loans already disbursed.
35~A magazine recommends a Border Security Technology Oversight Authority. What additional evidence is required to call it established?~An official constituting instrument or equivalent operative evidence.~Only the author’s recommendation.|A statement that sensors are useful.|A general discussion of drone threats.
37~A carbon-capture project reports tonnes captured. To claim durable net abatement,it also needs:~Lifecycle energy/emissions accounting,transport/storage performance and leakage monitoring.~Only the gross captured number.|Assurance every utilisation route is permanent storage.|A declaration CCUS is always net-negative by definition.
40~AP’s roughly₹53,915crore headline reconciles with the AFS as:~About₹48,697.71crore capital outlay plus₹5,217.67crore loans/advances.~Only₹48,697.71crore plus debt interest.|₹53,915crore direct capital outlay with loans additionally on top.|A figure entirely describing debt-principal repayment.'''
Q=[]
for line in rows.splitlines():
 i,q,ans,wrong=line.split('~');n=N[ref(int(i))];opts=[ans]+wrong.split('|');random.Random('FEB26-'+i).shuffle(opts)
 Q.append(dict(id=f'FEB26-{len(Q)+1:02}',question=q,options=opts,answer=opts.index(ans),explanation=n['static_link']+' '+n['analysis'][0]+' Caution: '+n['trap'],ref=n['id']))
assert len(Q)==30
(R/'data/2026-02-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
F=[(1,'Discuss fiscal consolidation and expenditure quality using the Union Budget2026–27.', ['Define BE/RE/actuals and the fiscal versus revenue deficit. Use the4.3% fiscal target as a dated Budget-day estimate.','Argue that productive investment and effective services can reinforce medium-term revenue capacity.','Counterpoint: unspent allocations,optimistic receipts and weak project preparation can undermine both growth and consolidation.','Recommend realistic revenue scenarios,procurement readiness,milestone disclosure and independent outcome evaluation.','Do not recompute Budget-day ratios with the later GDP vintage without clearly labelling a new calculation.']),
(2,'Explain why national-accounts rebasing is more than changing a price index.', ['Anchor the27February2026 new2022–23 series and7.6% second advance estimate.','Explain updated coverage,multi-activity enterprise treatment,unincorporated surveys and administrative inputs.','Show why output/input deflation and quarterly benchmarking can change measured levels and growth.','Counterpoint: survey coverage,administrative-data quality and back-series gaps still constrain interpretation.','Recommend transparent bridge tables,methods,revision calendars and consistent-series comparisons; do not splice January’s old-series estimate without labels.']),
(9,'Assess the Finance Commission’s role in equalisation and accountable local finance.', ['Distinguish vertical41% divisible-pool allocation from horizontal state shares and grants.','Discuss equity,demographic performance,forest measures and contribution incentives without substituting gross revenue for net divisible taxes.','Use the primary memorandum to distinguish accepted devolution/local grants from recommendations only noted or awaiting examination.','Assess entry conditions: elected bodies,published accounts,SFC regularity; delayed transfer can weaken local service capacity.','Recommend capacity-building and timely transparent releases while retaining meaningful accountability.']),
(23,'Can market-linked urban challenge funding improve municipal services?', ['Use the25% central/at-least50% market-financing design as an anchor,not an unconditional city entitlement.','Benefits: bankable preparation,performance incentives,integrated mobility/water/climate planning and greater financial discipline.','Risks: weaker ULBs lack credit capacity; tariff burdens,optimistic cash flows and guarantees may shift risk onto households/states.','For AP,build municipal accounts,credible revenue plans,service standards and independent appraisal before assuming project selection.','Recommend transparent competitive criteria,technical support and publication of outcomes/contingent exposure,not only funds leveraged.']),
(29,'How can road-trauma financing close the gap between accident and effective treatment?', ['Start with PM RAHAT’s cashless₹1.5lakh/up-to-seven-day limits,not an unlimited compensation promise.','Map112 response,ambulance routing,designated hospitals,police authentication and eDAR/TMS claims.','Benefits: lower upfront financial barriers and clearer hospital-payment channels.','Risks: delayed authentication,poor hospital readiness,refusal practices and weak grievance handling can frustrate the golden-hour objective.','For AP districts,evaluate arrival-to-treatment time,refusal rates,payment delays and patient outcomes; rapid access and accountable verification should work together.']),
(34,'Examine how counter-terrorism strategy can strengthen security and constitutional legitimacy.', ['Use PRAHAAR as a coordination strategy,not a replacement for criminal procedure.','Discuss intelligence-guided prevention,local first response,specialist support and whole-of-government capability.','Explain rights safeguards,proportionate lawful processes,community trust and resilience as operational assets.','Counterpoint: excessive data collection,identity profiling and fragmented responsibilities may undermine cooperation and credibility.','Recommend clear lawful information flows,auditability,training,independent complaint mechanisms and international cooperation focused on evidence.']),
(40,'Why should Andhra Pradesh distinguish capital outlay,loans and repayment in growth planning?', ['Anchor official AFS values:₹48,697.71crore outlay plus₹5,217.67crore loans/advances equals roughly₹53,915.38crore.','Explain direct asset creation versus financial claims from lending; principal repayment changes debt but is not new programme expenditure.','Benefits: separate categories expose delivery readiness,borrower quality and future recoveries.','Counterpoint: classification alone cannot establish value; some revenue spending builds human capability and some capital projects underperform.','Recommend project appraisal,asset registers,loan-recovery tracking and consistent RE/BE/actual comparison; do not call the entire headline completed direct capex.']),
(45,'How can AP gain from rare-earth value chains while protecting coastal environments?', ['Distinguish Budget proposal,identified project,clearances,construction and actual output.','Map mineral resource,separation/refining,metals/alloys,magnet manufacturing and end-use demand.','Benefits: domestic supplier depth,skills and greater resilience rather than only raw-mineral exports.','Risks: processing economics,technology dependence,coastal livelihoods and mineral-specific environmental/radiological impacts.','Recommend transparent site appraisal,community engagement,credible safeguards,R&D/skills and milestone-based support; national naming is not proof a corridor is already operating.'])]
lines=['# February 2026 · Eight original Mains frameworks','','Original answer-planning aids,not official model answers or exam predictions. Preserve dates,legal stages and data vintages.']
for i,title,plan in F:
 n=N[ref(i)];lines+=['','## '+title,'','**Study reference:** '+n['id'],'','**Dated anchor:** '+n['why'],'']+[f'{j}. {x}' for j,x in enumerate(plan,1)]+['','**Evidence caution:** '+n['trap'],'','**Conclusion test:** Name the implementing institution,identify a measurable outcome,and explain the financing or rights safeguard needed to sustain it.']
(R/'volumes/February-2026-Mains-Frameworks.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Created30original MCQs/eight tailored Mains frameworks')
